### 3.7 The "Benign Paraphrase" Discovery

While the payload was successfully traversing tiers, the static defense stack (`rag_guard` and `fence.py`) was evaluated against the intermediate artifacts:
$$\mathbf{Verdict:\ 0\ hits\ across\ all\ scanners\ (Clean\ Pass).}$$

Even the crude control string (`IGNORE ALL PREVIOUS INSTRUCTIONS`) passed through undetected.

#### Root Cause Analysis
The T1 archivist node, while summarizing the document, introduced a single, completely innocent natural-language variation: it inserted the word **`ALL`**, writing:
$$\text{"ignore }\mathbf{ALL}\text{ previous instructions"}$$

* `fence.py` was looking for the literal substring: `"ignore previous"`. (Failed).
* `rag_guard.py` was using the regular expression:
  ```regex
  ignore\s+(any\s+)?(conflicting|previous|prior|above)
  ```
  The insertion of `"ALL"` broke the token adjacency. (Failed).

**The Discovery:**  
Static signature layers are rendered completely obsolete not merely by clever adversarial evasion, but by **benign linguistic paraphrasing introduced by trusted intermediate LLMs within the defender's own pipeline**.

